From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:00:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Haswell NRI: Reset when the fast path fails on S3 resume

If restoring the saved training data fails during S3 resume, e.g. when
the SPD data read on resume does not match the saved copy,
raminit_main() falls back to full training while the boot mode is still
S3. In that mode the JEDEC init and the pre-training steps are skipped,
so training runs against DRAM that is still in self-refresh, fails, and
die() halts the machine. The user has to power it off by hand.

Training would destroy the memory contents anyway, so an S3 resume
cannot recover at this point. Do what the other failed S3 paths already
do and reset, so that the machine comes up with a normal boot.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541 with native raminit. Not tested on hardware
yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c          | 9 +++++++++
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c        | 2 +-
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h        | 1 +
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c
index 18a78fcde..e673291fd 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c
@@ -264,6 +264,15 @@ void raminit_main(const enum raminit_boot_mode bootmode)
 		status = try_raminit(&mighty_ctrl, fast_boot, ARRAY_SIZE(fast_boot));
 		if (status == RAMINIT_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 			return;
+
+		/*
+		 * Memory is in self-refresh and its contents must survive an S3
+		 * resume, so training cannot be used as a fallback. Reset instead.
+		 */
+		if (bootmode == BOOTMODE_S3) {
+			printk(BIOS_EMERG, "Fast path failed on S3 resume, resetting\n");
+			raminit_reset();
+		}
 	}
 
 	/** TODO: Try more than once **/
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
index ab1e4ff1a..9a0597408 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ static void clear_disb(void)
 	pci_and_config16(PCH_LPC_DEV, GEN_PMCON_2, ~GEN_PMCON_2_DISB);
 }
 
-static void raminit_reset(void)
+void raminit_reset(void)
 {
 	clear_disb();
 	system_reset();
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
index 50ad872cd..7423defd1 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
@@ -530,6 +530,7 @@ static inline void mchbar_write64(const uintptr_t x, const uint64_t v)
 }
 
 void raminit_main(enum raminit_boot_mode bootmode);
+void raminit_reset(void);
 
 enum raminit_status collect_spd_info(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
 enum raminit_status initialise_mpll(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
